WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:16.975
The Lemonade Detectives looked at Hannah in surprise.

2
00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:19.536
"Mrs. Sweet is dating Mr.

3
00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:21.057
Moss?" Maggie said.

4
00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:23.058
Hannah giggled.

5
00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:27.000
"My mom works at a fancy restaurant on Baker Street.

6
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.241
She says Mr.

7
00:00:29.321 --> 00:00:30.301
Moss and Mrs.

8
00:00:30.381 --> 00:00:32.882
Sweet have been there a lot recently."

9
00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:35.783
Henry was surprised by Hannah's news.

10
00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:37.264
Was it a clue?

11
00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:39.885
By now it was late afternoon.

12
00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:46.087
He looked over at the Dessert Den, and saw that the electrician's truck was still there.

13
00:00:47.148 --> 00:00:48.668
So they still couldn't talk to Mr.

14
00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:54.751
Tate. you know that Mrs.

15
00:00:54.831 --> 00:00:55.831
Sweet and Mr.

16
00:00:55.911 --> 00:00:56.992
Moss were dating?"

17
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.982
Henry asked his friends as they wandered toward their bikes.

18
00:01:00.002 --> 00:01:03.003
"Nope. Mr.

19
00:01:03.043 --> 00:01:06.866
Moss usually spreads around all the town gossip," Cole said with a smile.

20
00:01:06.886 --> 00:01:10.288
"I guess he doesn't like to gossip about himself though!"

21
00:01:10.308 --> 00:01:12.049
"Maybe Mr.

22
00:01:12.109 --> 00:01:17.072
Moss pushed over our bikes because he knew we were investigating his girlfriend," said Maggie.

23
00:01:17.092 --> 00:01:19.834
"Maybe," Henry said.

24
00:01:19.854 --> 00:01:21.174
"But Mr.

25
00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.075
Moss is just as nice as Mrs.

26
00:01:23.136 --> 00:01:28.229
Sweet. I can't believe he'd do something like that and then lie about it to us."

27
00:01:28.249 --> 00:01:29.989
"Me neither."

28
00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:30.990
Cole gulped.

29
00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.150
"Not unless he knows Mrs.

30
00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.551
Sweet is guilty, that is."

31
00:01:34.571 --> 00:01:37.471
"I have an idea," Henry said.

32
00:01:37.491 --> 00:01:39.772
"Let's go talk to my dad."

33
00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:41.613
Maggie groaned.

34
00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:44.173
"You want to ride back to town again?"

35
00:01:44.553 --> 00:01:45.053
she said.

36
00:01:45.073 --> 00:01:48.954
"Anyway, I thought you didn't want your dad to investigate Mrs.

37
00:01:48.994 --> 00:01:54.296
Sweet." "He's written a few stories about West Belltown," Henry reminded her.

38
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.581
"He might know something useful."

39
00:02:00.023 --> 00:02:01.624
They rode to the newspaper office.

40
00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:06.486
Henry's dad was in the reception area shuffling through some papers.

41
00:02:06.506 --> 00:02:09.088
"Hello, kids!"

42
00:02:09.488 --> 00:02:10.749
he greeted them with a smile.

43
00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:12.670
"What brings you here?"

44
00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.472
"We're working on a tough case," Henry said.

45
00:02:16.492 --> 00:02:19.654
"We were hoping we could talk to you about it."

46
00:02:19.674 --> 00:02:22.976
"Sure." Henry's dad checked his watch.

47
00:02:24.184 --> 00:02:25.985
"I have to go to a meeting in a few minutes.

48
00:02:26.085 --> 00:02:27.606
But we can talk until then."

49
00:02:32.889 --> 00:02:34.290
He led the way to his office.

50
00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:41.353
After he closed the door, Henry and his friends told him all about the mystery.

51
00:02:41.373 --> 00:02:44.755
"Wow," Henry's dad said when they finished.

52
00:02:44.775 --> 00:02:47.036
"That's quite a story."

53
00:02:47.056 --> 00:02:50.818
"You can't tell anyone, Uncle Kevin," Maggie said.

54
00:02:50.838 --> 00:02:52.599
"We don't want to ruin Mrs.

55
00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.720
Sweet's reputation."

56
00:02:55.028 --> 00:02:56.209
Henry's dad smiled.

57
00:02:56.229 --> 00:02:58.350
"I can keep a secret.

58
00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:03.973
But I'm sure the flavor theft is just some kind of misunderstanding."

59
00:03:03.993 --> 00:03:06.935
"I hope so," Henry said.

60
00:03:06.955 --> 00:03:09.176
"But how can we prove it?

61
00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:12.778
Do you have any information that could help us crack the case?"

62
00:03:12.798 --> 00:03:16.260
"I'm afraid not," his father said.

63
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.702
"But it sounds like you still have a few clues to investigate.

64
00:03:21.582 --> 00:03:24.104
Like the timing of the two signs, for instance."

65
00:03:25.268 --> 00:03:26.809
"Yeah." Cole bit his lip.

66
00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:29.070
"But what if we find out Mr.

67
00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.111
Tate had the flavor on his sign first?

68
00:03:32.052 --> 00:03:32.772
That means Mrs.

69
00:03:32.852 --> 00:03:33.773
Sweet is the culprit."

70
00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:35.814
Henry's dad shrugged.

71
00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:41.657
"Being a good detective, or a good reporter, means looking for the truth.

72
00:03:42.778 --> 00:03:47.220
You have to dig up all the facts, even if they lead to an answer you don't like."

73
00:03:48.341 --> 00:03:49.421
There was a knock on the door.

74
00:03:49.441 --> 00:03:52.723
"Time for the meeting, Kevin," a woman called.

75
00:03:52.743 --> 00:03:55.829
"Thanks." Henry's dad stood.

76
00:03:55.849 --> 00:03:57.990
"Sorry, kids.

77
00:03:58.390 --> 00:03:58.970
I have to go.

78
00:03:59.451 --> 00:04:01.132
We can talk more later if you like."

79
00:04:02.252 --> 00:04:03.873
"Okay. Thanks, Dad."

80
00:04:05.514 --> 00:04:08.416
As Henry and his friends left the building, someone stepped toward them.

81
00:04:09.276 --> 00:04:09.916
It was Robby.

82
00:04:09.936 --> 00:04:12.678
"Hi," Cole greeted him.

83
00:04:13.318 --> 00:04:14.199
"What are you doing here?"

84
00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.540
"Looking for you guys."

85
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.221
Robby looked miserable.

86
00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:20.542
"I need to apologize."

87
00:04:21.743 --> 00:04:22.383
"What for?"

88
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:23.444
asked Maggie.

89
00:04:24.412 --> 00:04:27.234
"For knocking over your bikes earlier," Robby said.

90
00:04:27.254 --> 00:04:29.135
"That was you?"

91
00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.336
Cole exclaimed.

92
00:04:30.356 --> 00:04:31.857
"Why'd you do it?"

93
00:04:31.877 --> 00:04:34.719
"I knew you were working for Mr.

94
00:04:34.759 --> 00:04:36.060
Tate," Robby said.

95
00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.063
"I'm mad at him because he ruined my parents' plans for a community garden.

96
00:04:42.144 --> 00:04:45.306
That's why I followed you to the Sweet Shop and knocked over your bikes."

97
00:04:46.507 --> 00:04:47.087
He sighed.

98
00:04:47.107 --> 00:04:52.551
"But when I told my dad what I did, he made me promise to find you and apologize.

99
00:04:53.291 --> 00:04:54.032
So I'm sorry."

100
00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.401
"It's okay," Henry said.

101
00:04:57.421 --> 00:04:59.861
"Are your parents mad at Mr.

102
00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:00.521
Tate too?"

103
00:05:00.541 --> 00:05:06.483
"I thought they were, but Dad says he's glad our neighborhood is getting some new businesses."

104
00:05:07.444 --> 00:05:08.144
Robby shrugged.

105
00:05:08.164 --> 00:05:10.224
"Maybe I am too.

106
00:05:11.265 --> 00:05:13.965
It might be cool to have a dessert place a few blocks from home."

107
00:05:14.946 --> 00:05:16.426
Robby said good-bye and moved on.

108
00:05:16.446 --> 00:05:20.327
"I guess that solves one mystery," Cole said.

109
00:05:20.347 --> 00:05:26.530
"Yeah. But it doesn't help with identifying the flavor thief," Henry said.

110
00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.931
"Or with clearing Mrs.

111
00:05:29.012 --> 00:05:29.792
Sweet's name."

112
00:05:29.812 --> 00:05:33.154
"I know how to do that," Maggie said.

113
00:05:33.174 --> 00:05:34.935
"We need to talk to Mr.

114
00:05:34.955 --> 00:05:36.195
Tate about that sign!"

115
00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.837
This time it was Cole who groaned.

116
00:05:38.857 --> 00:05:41.979
"It's getting late," he said.

117
00:05:41.999 --> 00:05:45.260
"Plus, Nathan's still selling lemonade for us.

118
00:05:46.001 --> 00:05:48.542
Do we really have to ride to West Belltown again?"

119
00:05:48.562 --> 00:05:51.524
"Yes!" Maggie insisted.

120
00:05:52.244 --> 00:05:52.824
"Come on!"

121
00:05:54.425 --> 00:05:56.326
She hopped on her bike and rode down the street.

122
00:06:00.869 --> 00:06:02.309
But suddenly she stopped short.

123
00:06:02.329 --> 00:06:04.351
"What is it?"

124
00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.031
Henry asked as he caught up.

125
00:06:06.051 --> 00:06:09.273
"Look!" Maggie pointed to Mrs.

126
00:06:09.293 --> 00:06:10.134
Sweet's flavor board.

127
00:06:10.154 --> 00:06:14.196
"Bubble gum banana swirl is gone!"
